Package: whatsappaudioR
Title: Convert Compressed Mobile Voice Notes into Tidy Spectrogram Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Anirjit", "Deb Adhikary", email = "adhikaryanirjit05@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Charitha", "Vaddi", role = "aut"))
URL: https://github.com/jitu-droid/sonicscout
BugReports: https://github.com/jitu-droid/sonicscout/issues
Description: Reads compressed '.opus' and '.ogg' voice notes, the kind
    produced by 'WhatsApp' and similar messaging apps, and converts them
    directly into tidy data frames of spectrogram and spectral-feature data,
    ready for analysis or modeling. Also provides a function to simulate the
    lossy compression such apps apply, for testing how well a signal
    survives it. Decoding and compression use a system 'FFmpeg' installation
    with 'libopus' support. Built for a bioacoustic pest-detection pipeline
    ('SonicScout') but has no dependency on that domain.
